                            <comment id="496621" author="JIRAUSER19573" created="Mon, 22 Jun 2026 22:09:37 +0000">&lt;p&gt; The issue for OST_WRITE described in &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-15863" class="external-link" rel="nofollow"&gt;LU-15863&lt;/a&gt;is already taken care of by this below patch - &lt;br/&gt;
&lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/45459" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/45459&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;But this fix looks like wouldn't cover the race for OST_SETATTR.&lt;/p&gt;


&lt;div class="code panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="codeContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre class="code-java"&gt;
&lt;span class="code-keyword"&gt;static&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="code-object"&gt;int&lt;/span&gt; ofd_setattr_hdl() {
....
....
    fo = ofd_object_find_exists(tsi-&amp;gt;tsi_env, ofd, &amp;amp;tsi-&amp;gt;tsi_fid);
    &lt;span class="code-keyword"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; (IS_ERR(fo))
	GOTO(out, rc = PTR_ERR(fo));

    la_from_obdo(&amp;amp;fti-&amp;gt;fti_attr, &amp;amp;body-&amp;gt;oa, body-&amp;gt;oa.o_valid);
    fti-&amp;gt;fti_attr.la_valid &amp;amp;= ~LA_TYPE;    &lt;span class="code-comment"&gt;/* setting objects attributes (including owner/group) */&lt;/span&gt;

    rc = ofd_attr_set(tsi-&amp;gt;tsi_env, fo, &amp;amp;fti-&amp;gt;fti_attr, &amp;amp;body-&amp;gt;oa);
    &lt;span class="code-keyword"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; (rc != 0)
        GOTO(out_put, rc);
...
....
}&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In OST_SETATTR case, if the object is missing during replay, it can return &lt;tt&gt;-ENOENT&lt;/tt&gt; before &lt;tt&gt;ofd_attr_set()&lt;/tt&gt; is ever called. And there is no guarantee that this request will first go through the LVB init path that has the &lt;tt&gt;EINPROGRESS&lt;/tt&gt; retry logic.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;OST_SETATTR &lt;b&gt;doesn't&lt;/b&gt; have an explicit recreate/retry logic like ofd_prepwr_write() that forces the write replay and thus leverages the fix through ofd_lvb change in the above patch.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
